  "title": "STM32L496RGT6 taking more current while programming on 1.8V",
  "content": "<p>Hi,</p><p>We are using STM32L496RGT6, VDD voltage is 1.8V, our device is low power device, max current available on 1.8V is 13mA. </p><p>We are using Segger flasher for flashing .hex file to MCU by SWD and Speed 4000kHz. </p><p>Now while flashing MCU, it takes around 36mA current. </p><p>Setting as follows, can we reduce programming power by changing any setting in flasher tool. </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/a2c00fa4-4843-4a10-a9b7-b9e8bb457ea1.png\" /></figure><p> </p>",
